---
import JobsWorkbenchDemo from './JobsWorkbenchDemo.astro';
---
<section class="ls-container ls-jobs-episode" id="jobs-workbench" aria-labelledby="jobs-workbench-title">
  <div class="ls-jobs-intro">
    <div><p class="ls-eyebrow">JOBS LIVE IN THE DOCUMENT</p>
      <h2 id="jobs-workbench-title">NEW NUMBERS IN.<br/><span class="ls-stroke">YOUR CALL ON WHAT STAYS.</span></h2></div>
    <div class="ls-episode-dek"><p>Monthly work should not start from a blank page. A document can carry its own Jobs: gather the new figures, redraw the table and chart, draft what changed. In our client brief walk, the table redrew in under half a second.</p>
    <p>Then you review one part at a time. <span class="flow-term">Keep</span> records your decision. <span class="flow-term">Revert</span> restores that part. <span class="flow-term">Later</span> leaves it applied, ready for your return.</p></div>
  </div>
  <JobsWorkbenchDemo />
  <p class="ls-jobs-caption">Add interview I12, run Research Refresh, then open the changed table and chart.</p>
</section>
